     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Asha ate 1 and 1/2 rotis. Her brother ate 3/4 of a roti.\n\"How much in all?\" asked her mother."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "mixed fraction",
     "like fractions",
     "numerator"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "A mixed fraction has a whole part and a fraction part, such as 1 and 1/2, which is the same as 3/2.\nTo add fractions with the same denominator, add the numerators: 1/4 plus 2/4 is 3/4. To subtract, subtract the numerators: 3/4 minus 1/4 is 2/4, or 1/2.\nIf denominators differ, we first make them equal using equivalent fractions."
    }
   },
